# Every service Dockerfile takes the REPO ROOT as its build context (each one
# copies only the subtrees it needs), so this single file governs all of them.
# Each Dockerfile's COPY list is the real scoping mechanism; this exists to keep
# the context transfer from shipping hundreds of megabytes of build output.

.git
.github

# goreleaser output — the largest thing in the tree by far (piri's binary alone
# is ~68MB), and never an input to a build.
**/dist/

# Editor and local state
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/node_modules/

# smelt's committed snapshot fixtures and generated compose are runtime test
# data, not build inputs. ingot's image copies smelt/ for its replace target and
# would otherwise drag these along.
smelt/snapshots/
smelt/generated/

# Docs site and OpenTofu deployment configs: not inputs to any binary.
piri/docs/
piri/deploy/

# The workspace file is deliberately excluded: container builds must resolve
# exactly what a GOWORK=off build resolves, through go.mod and its replace
# directives. See the header comment in each Dockerfile.
go.work
go.work.sum
